d specified weighted norms. It does not imply global operator-norm convergence, a nondegenerate covariance assumption, or uniformity in growing word length.","citation_ids":["circuit-r2-26-cite-weighted-unitary-calculus"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"circuit.weighted_unitary_calculus","kind":"claim","label":"Weighted sums, products and commuting substitution","locator":"02-foundations.tex:367–950; lem:weyl-bounds, lem:centered-sums, lem:unitary-clt, lem:commuting-substitution","source_id":"circuit-r2-26-source-foundations","statement":"For fixed finite recursively weighted smooth families, with corresponding adjoint jets controlled, centered normalized sums and products of small unitaries admit the stated rooted limits. The product limit retains the imaginary scalar second-derivative correction. Jointly strongly commuting controls may be substituted when joint exponentials and coefficient/adjoint jets have polynomial weighted bounds; Fourier tails are controlled before removing the cutoff.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/circuit.weighted_unitary_calculus","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/circuit.gate_calculus","id":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/edges/%5B%22circuit.gate_calculus%22%2C%22circuit.weighted_unitary_calculus%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","kind":"supports","record_ref":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/edges/%5B%22circuit.gate_calculus%22%2C%22circuit.weighted_unitary_calculus%22%2C%22supports%22%5D","semantic_class":"curated_argument_support","to":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/circuit.weighted_unitary_calculus"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:3592e6a1f4e5ac9cf05e86d1dac98fabd5ac5f25ba57c4ce6e79c2b2f110d0db/nodes/circuit.ordinary_updates",